# Free play, the SMK-37's top pad 7 (index 6): the keys play one GM sound with the band stopped, the screen names the
# note, the interval or the chord. Only the sound is kept: the songs, the band and every other setting are as before.
# (a shot waits for the screen's next frames; page 18: P_FREE; free_chord: root*100 + CH_* type, C major 0, Am7 918)
wait 300
snap
expect page 0
pad 6
expect page 18
wait 80
shot free_empty.png
# ---- a note: C4 (keybed key 12)
kbkey 12 down 100
expect free_n 1
expect free_low 60
wait 80
shot free_note.png
# ---- a chord: C E G, then let go (the last stays, dim)
kbkey 16 down 100
kbkey 19 down 100
expect free_n 3
expect free_chord 0
wait 80
shot free_chord.png
kbkey 12 up
kbkey 16 up
kbkey 19 up
expect free_n 0
expect free_chord 0
wait 80
shot free_last.png
# ---- Am7: A3 C4 E4 G4
kbkey 9 down 90
kbkey 12 down 90
kbkey 16 down 90
kbkey 19 down 90
expect free_chord 918
expect free_low 57
wait 80
shot free_am7.png
kbkey 9 up
kbkey 12 up
kbkey 16 up
kbkey 19 up
# ---- two notes: C4 and G4, their interval
kbkey 12 down 100
kbkey 19 down 100
expect free_n 2
wait 80
shot free_interval.png
kbkey 12 up
kbkey 19 up
# ---- the sound (K5 here: the simulator's K1), the volume (K2), a family on (PRESET)
spin K1 5
expect free_prog 5
spin K2 -20
expect free_vol 80
wait 80
shot free_sound.png
spin PRESET 1
expect free_prog 8
# ---- its own octave: OCT+ moves the keys here, not the project's octave
tap OCT+
kbkey 12 down 100
expect free_low 72
kbkey 12 up
tap OCT-
# ---- the staff: the black keys by the chord's key (Eb major: flats; D major: sharps)
kbkey 15 down 100
kbkey 19 down 100
kbkey 22 down 100
expect free_chord 300
expect free_flats 1
wait 80
shot free_staff_eb.png
kbkey 15 up
kbkey 19 up
kbkey 22 up
kbkey 14 down 100
kbkey 18 down 100
kbkey 21 down 100
expect free_chord 200
expect free_flats 0
wait 80
shot free_staff_d.png
kbkey 14 up
kbkey 18 up
kbkey 21 up
# a 2nd and ledger lines: C3 D3 (low) and C6 (high), the notes beside each other
kbkey 0 down 100
kbkey 2 down 100
kbkey 36 down 100
wait 80
shot free_staff_ledger.png
kbkey 0 up
kbkey 2 up
kbkey 36 up
# past the ledger lines: three octaves up, C9: an octave in, 8va
tap OCT+
tap OCT+
tap OCT+
kbkey 36 down 100
expect free_low 120
wait 80
shot free_staff_8va.png
kbkey 36 up
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
# KNOB 4 (the simulator's K4): flats; KNOB 3: the staff off (the names alone, large)
spin K4 2
expect free_flats 1
kbkey 13 down 100
wait 80
shot free_staff_flat.png
kbkey 13 up
spin K3 -1
expect free_staff 0
wait 80
shot free_nostaff.png
spin K3 1
spin K4 -2
# ---- the band's controls do nothing here
pad 0
pad 8
expect page 18
fader 0 10
fader 1 120
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
tap REC
expect recording 0
tap SEL
sbtn KNOB_BANK
expect smkmap 0
spin SELECT 1
spin ALGO 1
expect page 18
# ---- out: pad 7 again, back where it was; nothing else changed
pad 6
expect page 0
expect unchanged 1
expect free_prog 8
# ---- from the Song page, PATCH (HOME) out to Home
tap HOME
expect page 1
pad 6
expect page 18
tap HOME
expect page 0
expect unchanged 1
